    "result": "I added Pix and made each method its own type, but I could not run the tests. The environment blocked `go test` and `git rm`.\n\n- **`method.go`:** the `Method` interface, the four constructors and the `Label()` methods. `Method` has a private `fee` method, so only this package can make a `Method`. Each constructor returns `(nil, ErrInvalid)` for a bad value.\n- **`fees.go`:** now holds `Fee(m, cents)`, which calls each type's own fee. Pix's fee is 0.\n- **`validate.go`:** keeps `ErrInvalid` and the digit and email checks. I removed `Validate` and `ErrKind`, since there is no longer an unknown kind to reject.\n- **`method_test.go`:** new. It checks the fee and label for each method, and the invalid inputs.\n\nCard, SEPA and PayPal keep their current checks, fees and labels. SEPA still checks the uppercased IBAN but builds its label from the original, as before. A Pix key is not stripped of spaces, because the spec did not ask for that.\n\n**TLDR**\nPix is added and each method is its own type, but nothing has been run. Run `go vet ./... \u0026\u0026 go test ./...` to check it.",
